# `~/.claude/settings.json` is a symlink to claude/settings.json, so Claude Code
# writes straight through into this repo. It re-adds `enabledPlugins` on every
# plugin enable/disable and `model`/`effortLevel` on /model and /config changes —
# machine-local state that must never be committed, or a fresh clone inherits
# this machine's plugin/model/effort choices. `autoMode` (the classifier
# customization block, hand-edited per project) gets the same treatment since
# it's just as machine/project-specific. The clean filter strips these keys at
# stage time, so they can live in the working file while staying out of every
# commit, and `git status` stays quiet. `jq -S` also absorbs Claude Code's key
# reordering. install.sh configures the filter; git will not do it from a clone.
claude/settings.json filter=claude-settings
